# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Permits authorized in Greater Houston, from the Census Building Permits Survey.

One quantity lives in this file and it is not the one in market.py. Census counts
housing units AUTHORISED BY PERMIT. That is phase one of five in the Census
definition of new residential construction; it is not a start, not a completion,
and not a closing. The closings figures on the deck come from builders and count
houses handed over. The two are never added, divided or drawn on one axis.

Retrieval: HUD's SOCDS query tool, which republishes the Census Building Permits
Survey at metro, county and permit-issuing jurisdiction level. Query run
2026-09-12: geography Houston-Pasadena-The Woodlands CBSA 26420, periodicity
Annual, series Single Family and All Permits.

Integrity: the 122 jurisdictions sum exactly to the ten counties, and the ten
counties sum exactly to the metro, in every year of overlap. Zero difference, not
rounded agreement. The build fails if that stops being true.

Nothing here is estimated. A year a source does not publish is absent, not zero.
"""

